---
import { ISSUES_URL, LICENSE_URL, REPO_URL } from '../config'
import Document from '../layouts/Document.astro'

// Security problems go to GitHub's private vulnerability reporting, which the policy explains.
const reportUrl = `${REPO_URL}/security/advisories/new`
const securityPolicyUrl = `${REPO_URL}/blob/main/.github/SECURITY.md`
---

<Document
  title="Disclaimer · FXM"
  description="FXM is an independent open-source project, not affiliated with or endorsed by YouTube, Google, Spotify or any music service. Provided as is, for personal use."
  heading="Disclaimer"
  lead="FXM is an independent, open-source music player. Here is what that means for you."
  updated="2026-10-26"
>
  <h2>An independent project</h2>
  <p>
    FXM is an independent open-source project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored
    by YouTube, Google, Spotify or any other music service.
  </p>

  <h2>A player, not a music service</h2>
  <p>
    FXM doesn't host or distribute any music, and it has no servers of its own. The apps run on your
    device and connect it directly to the music services FXM works with.
  </p>

  <h2>Provided as is, for personal use</h2>
  <p>
    FXM is provided “as is”, without warranties or conditions of any kind, as described in the
    <a href={LICENSE_URL}>Apache License 2.0</a>. It is meant for personal use.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for how you use FXM, including following the terms of the services you use
    with it and the laws where you live. Nothing on this website is legal advice: if you aren't sure
    what is allowed, read those terms or ask a lawyer.
  </p>

  <h2>Trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    YouTube and Google are trademarks of Google LLC. Spotify is a trademark of Spotify AB. All other
    trademarks belong to their respective owners. FXM names these services only to say which ones it
    works with, and doesn't use their logos or brand colours.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Notices and takedown requests.</strong>
      If you think FXM or this website infringes your rights, open an issue on the
      <a href={ISSUES_URL}>FXM issue tracker on GitHub</a>
      and say which part of FXM it is about. Issues are public, so leave out anything you don't want
      published.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Security problems.</strong>
      Please don't report them in a public issue. Report them privately through
      <a href={reportUrl}>GitHub's private vulnerability reporting</a>, as the
      <a href={securityPolicyUrl}>FXM security policy</a>
      describes.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Document>
